  "contentHtml": "\n                                    \n\n                                                                            <p><img src=\"https://health.economictimes.indiatimes.com/Themes/Release/theme4/images/icons/et-default-user.svg\" alt=\"Teena Thacker\">\n                                            \n                                        </p>\n                                                                        \n                                                                                    <ul>\n                                                                                                    <li>\n                                                                                                                                                                            <a>Teena Thacker</a>\n                                                            \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        \n                                                                                                            </li>\n                                                                                                                                                    <li><a href=\"/agency/88675387/ET-Bureau\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ET Bureau</a></li>\n                                                                                            </ul>\n                                                                                <ul>\n                                                                                            <li>Published On Oct 15, 2026 at 07:33 AM IST</li>\n                                                                                                                                            <li>\n                                                        \n                                                            \n                                                                Read by \n                                                            \n                                                            100 Professionals\n                                                        \n                                                    </li>\n                                                                                    </ul>\n                                    \n                                                                            \n                                                                        \n                                \n                                \n\n                    <!-- Display video article in news article for the custom next story -->\n                    \n                    <!-- Modifying the body placing embeds,promoslots,related etc.-->\n                                        <figure><img src=\"/images/default.jpg\" alt=\"\"></figure><p>New Delhi: The cabinet secretariat asked the Union health ministry to take action on concerns over the safety and quality of coronary stents, after a Parliament member sought its intervention.In a representation to the cabinet secretariat, Rajya Sabha member <a href=\"/tag/ajeet+madhavrao+gopchade\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ajeet Madhavrao Gopchade</a>, a medical doctor, flagged safety concerns involving three models of India-made, drug-eluting coronary stents that were reportedly withdrawn in Sri Lanka following quality issues.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>In his representation, the MP referred to media reports of Sri Lanka's medical device regulator directing the withdrawal of the three stent models due to concerns over improper positioning, stent dislodgement, acute stent thrombosis and failure to expand properly. The concerns were identified during an investigation by the <a href=\"/tag/medical+device+evaluation+committee\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">medical device evaluation committee</a>, according to the reports.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M -->\n                            <p>Advt\n                            </p>\n\n                              \n                                                         \n                        <p>\"These reports highlight certain patient-safety issues that India needs to examine carefully and address proactively,\" he said in his September 29 representation, a copy of which ET has seen. The cabinet secretariat's direction to the health ministry came on October 5.The MP urged the government to examine whether India's existing regulatory framework for coronary stents required further strengthening, emphasising the need for appropriate clinical decision-making, rigorous device testing and effective monitoring of complications after implantation.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><h2><strong>Mechanism Needed</strong></h2><p>He called for better clinical documentation to ensure that stents are used only when medically indicated and that alternative treatments are considered wherever appropriate. The MP also proposed robust batch and serial-number traceability for every implanted stent, alongside stronger <a href=\"/tag/post-market+surveillance\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">post-market surveillance</a> and adverse-event reporting.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>He urged the government to put in place a mechanism for promptly reviewing safety alerts, recalls and withdrawals issued by foreign regulators when the same or similar devices are marketed or used in India. The representation highlighted the need for appropriate patient follow-up and long-term safety data to identify potential device-related problems at an early stage.                    </p><!-- Category Most Read Placement -->\n                                                                    \n                                                                \n                                <ul>\n                                                                            <!-- <li>By <span>Teena Thacker</span>,</li> -->\n                                    \n\n                                                                            <li>By\n                                                                                            <a>Teena Thacker</a>\n\n                                                                                                                                                                                        , \n                                                                                    </li>\n                                                                        <li><a href=\"/agency/88675387/ET-Bureau\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ET Bureau</a></li>\n                                </ul>\n                                <ul>\n                                    <!-- <li> Updated On Oct 15, 2026 at 07:33 AM IST</li> -->\n                                    <li>Published On Oct 15, 2026 at 07:33 AM IST</li>\n                                    <!-- <li class=\"desktop-view\">2 min read</li> -->\n                                </ul>\n                            \n                                        \n\n                    \n\n                    <!-- Comment Section -->\n                                            \n                                        <!-- Comment Section -->\n\n                    \n                      \n    \n            <p>\n                </p><h2>Join the community of 2M+ industry professionals. </h2>   \n                <h3>Subscribe to Newsletter to get latest insights &amp; analysis in your inbox.</h3>\n            <p></p>\n\n            <!-- <figure class=\"top-newsletter-subs__icon-nl\" role=\"presentation\" aria-label=\"Newsletter icon\">\n                <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://st.etb2bimg.com/